  "notes": "Source: official 2024-2025 Bastyr University catalog page for the Doctor of Naturopathic Medicine (quarter system; 14 quarters sequenced Fall/Winter/Spring Year I-II, Summer/Fall/Winter/Spring Year III-IV, exactly as the catalog's quarterly tables print them). The catalog's published graduation total is 300 credits = 238.5 core + 8 elective + 53.5 clinic. This seed sequences every quarterly table at its printed total; third-year 'Clinic Rotation (1 or 2)' rows print a 2-4 credit range and are sequenced at the 2-credit minimum, and the 8 elective credits are not assigned to any quarter in the catalog, so total_credits (286) is the sum of sequenced course credits only. The catalog's quarterly rotation rows carry no course numbers (coded CLINIC-ROTATION here); its Summary of Clinic Requirements assigns third-year rotations to course series NM7851-7866 (patient care, 20 cr) and PM7851-7866 (physical medicine, 4 cr), and fourth-year rotations to NM8851-8866 (16 cr) and PM8851-8866 (4 cr). Catalog typo: the Electives Requirements paragraph prints '299.5 credit totals' while the Graduation Requirements and Total Requirements table both print 300. Scheduling notes from the catalog: BC5142 is offered summer and winter; NM5820 is also offered winter or spring; NM6810 is also offered in summer; NM7142 may also be offered spring quarter. Graduation: competency (grade of AC) in all 300 credits, all required clinical competencies, minimum 1,204 clinical hours, at least two-thirds of credits in residence, completion within six years. [Coordinator 2026-10-01: CLINIC-ROTATION placeholder genuinely repeats across terms (catalog-worded clinic rotations); pipeline-excluded by build.py's duplicate-course-code gate.]",
